    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThis PR makes `--enable-deterministic-inference` on ROCm refuse `--disable-custom-all-reduce` when `--tp-size` is above 2. That combination sends every tensor-parallel all-reduce through RCCL, which is not batch-invariant at four or more ranks: the server starts normally, but a request's output depends on what else is in its batch.\n\nOn ROCm, deterministic mode relies on SGLang's one-stage custom all-reduce, in which every rank reduces all inputs in a fixed order. CUDA instead disables the custom all-reduce and pins NCCL (tree algorithm, fixed channel count); ROCm has no such pinning, and pinning RCCL's algorithm and protocol (`NCCL_ALGO=Ring NCCL_PROTO=Simple`) does not make it batch-invariant either (results below). At TP2 each output element is the sum of two operands, which has only one order, and RCCL passes every check there, so TP2 stays allowed.\n\nImpact: only ROCm users who pass both flags with `--tp-size` above 2. They now get a startup error instead of silently batch-dependent results; dropping `--disable-custom-all-reduce` fixes it.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `arg_groups/overrides.py`: a validation pass, `_deterministic_rocm_rccl_check`, raises a `ValueError` for deterministic mode + ROCm + `tp_size > 2` + `disable_custom_all_reduce`.\n- `arg_groups/attention_hook.py`: runs it in the ROCm branch of the existing tensor-parallel check in `handle_deterministic_inference`.\n- `test/registered/unit/test_model_overrides.py`: two CPU cases. One for the refusal; one for the setups it must leave alone (CUDA, deterministic mode off, TP2, custom all-reduce on).\n- Unchanged: deterministic mode without the flag, TP1 and TP2, CUDA, and everything without `--enable-deterministic-inference`.\n\nIndependent of #34543, which makes the custom all-reduce itself batch-invariant for inputs larger than its buffer.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n**Why RCCL is refused.** Qwen3-8B, BF16, `SGLANG_USE_AITER=0 python3 -m sglang.launch_server --model-path Qwen/Qwen3-8B --tp <N> --attention-backend triton --enable-deterministic-inference --disable-custom-all-reduce`, `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.21-rocm724-mi35x-20261006`. Checks: `python3 -m sglang.test.test_deterministic --test-mode prefix --return-logprob` and `--test-mode radix_cache` (50 trials), plus a bitwise comparison of 1,275 responses (batch sizes 1-50) against batch size 1.\n\n| RCCL setting | GPU | TP2 | TP4 | TP8 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| default | MI350X | pass all | fail all | - |\n| default | MI355X | pass all | fail all (81/1275 bitwise-identical) | - |\n| `NCCL_ALGO=Ring NCCL_PROTO=Simple` | MI355X | pass all | fail all (347/1275) | fail all (121/1275) |\n\n**This PR.** MI350X, `rocm/sgl-dev:v0.5.21-rocm724-mi35x-20261011`, the image's files before and with this change.\n\n| Deterministic, `--attention-backend triton` | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| TP2, TP4, TP8 | accepted | accepted |\n| TP2 + `--disable-custom-all-reduce` | accepted | accepted; the server starts and generates |\n| TP4 or TP8 + `--disable-custom-all-reduce` | accepted | `ValueError` at startup |\n\n- Checked with `ServerArgs.resolve_once()` for all six combinations, and with `launch_server` for TP2 and TP4.\n- The new test cases pass, and every other test in `test_model_overrides.py` has the same outcome with and without this PR.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo performance effect: this is a startup-time argument check.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38228603684](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38228603684)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38228603022](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38228603022)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38228603375](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38228603375)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
